-- 0010_chart_lab_seed_drills.sql — A Girl & Her Futures™
--
-- Seeds the same 11 starter drills already reviewed and shipped as Chart
-- Lab's client-side demo-mode fixtures (agihf/shared/chartlab-service.js's
-- demoDrills array) as REAL, published rows, so a real member account
-- shows a working "Today's Drill" / "Browse by Skill" home page instead of
-- an empty "Nothing recommended yet" state on day one.
--
-- WHY THIS EXISTS: 0009_chart_lab.sql only creates the Chart Lab tables —
-- it has zero INSERT statements. The 11 starter drills described in the
-- original Chart Lab spec have only ever existed as demo-mode fixtures,
-- never as real database rows, so every real account starts with zero
-- published drills until an admin manually creates some through the Admin
-- Chart Lab Builder. This migration is that missing seed step.
--
-- Every row here is marked is_seed_placeholder = true, which
-- admin-chart-lab.html already renders as a visible amber warning banner
-- ("This is dev/seed placeholder content — replace the chart image with a
-- real AGHF-owned chart..."). Chart images are the exact same generated
-- placeholder candlestick SVGs (as inline data: URIs, not real chart
-- screenshots) already used in demo mode — reused verbatim, not
-- reinvented, so demo mode and a fresh real account look identical until
-- an admin uploads real AGHF-owned charts.
--
-- Content (title, question, answer key, explanation, common mistake,
-- hints, related Dayli ICC rule) is copied field-for-field from
-- chartlab-service.js's demoDrills — already-reviewed member-facing copy,
-- not newly authored here.
--
-- Chart images are stored directly as data: URIs in chart_image_path
-- rather than real win-media Storage paths — a plain SQL migration can't
-- upload to Storage, and this sandbox has no live credentials to run a
-- seed script against a real project either. A matching one-line client
-- fix (chartlab-service.js's resolveChartImageUrl) recognizes a
-- chart_image_path that starts with "data:" and returns it directly
-- without attempting a Storage signed-URL lookup. When an admin later
-- uploads a real chart image for one of these drills through the existing
-- Admin Chart Lab Builder upload flow, chart_image_path becomes a genuine
-- "chartlab/..." Storage path again and the existing signed-URL path
-- takes back over automatically — no cleanup needed for that transition.
--
-- Purely additive data (no schema change) — must be applied AFTER
-- 0009_chart_lab.sql. Idempotent: safe to paste into the Supabase SQL
-- editor more than once (ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING on both tables).
--
-- HOW TO APPLY: paste into the Supabase SQL editor after 0009_chart_lab.sql
-- has already been run — same as every other migration in this project
-- (this sandbox has no live Supabase credentials to run it automatically).

insert into chart_lab_drills (
  id, title, description, drill_type, skill_category,
  difficulty, access_tier, practice_mode,
  phase_key, section_key, lesson_key, instrument, timeframe, historical_date,
  chart_format, chart_image_path, chart_image_width, chart_image_height, chart_alt_text,
  question, estimated_seconds, related_next_drill_id,
  status, version, is_seed_placeholder, created_by, published_at
) values
